        "content": "{\"original_question\":\"I'm considering whether I should start scripting my cooking videos or just go with the flow. What do you think?\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"What are the user's current constraints or goals (e.g., time, audience, quality) that might influence the scripting decision?\",\"output_slot\":\"current_constraints\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[],\"execution\":\"retrieval\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"What are the user's current constraints or goals (e.g., time, audience, quality) that might influence the scripting decision?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"4fc38374e5b3588f01f18b1a3cdb0d0d77578c309cc204ec50f04c1bcb334e69\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"23c8341d5d524bcf17f58ddade3966e85462ab8b9a9a2cc5ea4b3ccfa0633a2b\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"7c70cd9fbbbc0502848f9a1a941f73cb8341a22129c4364d7602f07b9036937a\"},\"variables\":{\"current_constraints\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"current_constraints\",\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"current_constraints\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"current_constraints\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[{\"id\":\"fact_fde86a26e64f6b0b731d2b8f\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user values creative freedom and spontaneity over rigid structures. They have repeatedly abandoned or disliked formal, structured creative formats (book reviews, blogging, fan fiction) because they felt stifling, chore-like, or limiting to their authentic expression. They prefer fluid, informal, and spontaneous forms of engagement (discussions, conversations) that allow genuine enthusiasm and authentic voice to lead. They have also found overwhelming fast-paced, high-pressure formats (live stream shopping) exhausting and frustrating. These experiences suggest a current constraint: the user is likely to prefer a flexible, unstructured, and low-pressure approach to scripting cooking videos, valuing authenticity and enjoyment over rigid planning or audience pressure.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s14\",\"s32\",\"s57\",\"s3\",\"s59\",\"s30\",\"s58\",\"s4\",\"s31\",\"s13\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's own statements across multiple conversations consistently express a dislike for structured, formal creative tasks (reviews, blogging, fan fiction) and a preference for spontaneous, fluid expression (discussions). They also describe feeling overwhelmed by fast-paced, high-pressure formats (live stream shopping). These are current, self-reported constraints and preferences that directly inform the scripting decision.\",\"variable\":\"current_constraints\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,457,\"User: I also abandoned the idea of writing reviews. I feel that they tend to limit my creativity, as if I am being boxed into a particular format that doesn't allow my thoughts to flow freely. There's something inherently stifling about structuring my feelings and opinions into a rigid framework, filled with guidelines about what to include or omit. \",\"user\",[53]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",457,790,\"Discussions, however, offer a much more fluid space where I can articulate my thoughts just as they come, allowing for spontaneity and genuine enthusiasm to take the lead. It’s fascinating how shifting my focus from written critiques to engaging dialogues can unleash a more authentic appreciation for the literary works that I love.\",\"user\",[53]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",105,455,\"User: I even started a blog about book reviews, but I lost interest quickly. It felt more like a chore at times. I had all these grand ideas about expressing my thoughts on various novels and sharing them with potential readers. However, as the weeks went by, the excitement fizzled out, and it became daunting to even consider writing another post. \",\"user\",[32]],[\"s14\",\"d2\",455,723,\"The joy I initially felt while discussing character arcs and plot twists was overshadowed by the pressure to consistently produce content. It was as if the very act of sharing my passion had turned into an obligation that drained my enthusiasm rather than igniting it.\",\"user\",[32]],[\"s30\",\"d3\",105,381,\"User: I even dabbled in writing fan fiction but felt it didn’t match my personal writing style anymore. I used to enjoy immersing myself in those universes, creating new scenarios and plots that brought my favorite characters to life in ways that hadn’t been explored before. \",\"user\",[40]],[\"s31\",\"d3\",381,768,\"However, as I continued to write, I began to notice a disconnect; my voice seemed to evolve, shifting towards a style that felt more unique to me, and I no longer felt that fan fiction was a suitable canvas. I often found myself reflecting on how fan fiction can be a stepping stone for many writers, allowing them to practice their craft in familiar settings while honing their skills. \",\"user\",[40]],[\"s32\",\"d3\",768,917,\"This journey made me appreciate the nuances of my own writing even more, as I sought to explore original ideas that resonated with my authentic self.\",\"user\",[40]],[\"s57\",\"d4\",107,374,\"User: However, I tried engaging in a live stream shopping event but found it overwhelming. The sheer volume of products being showcased was staggering, as dozens of items flashed across the screen, each promising to be the next must-have gadget or fashion statement. \",\"user\",[120]],[\"s58\",\"d4\",374,716,\"I struggled to keep up with the fast-paced commentary from the hosts, who seemed to effortlessly highlight product features while interacting with viewers in the chat. It felt like there was a pressure to make instantaneous decisions about purchases, which is not an easy feat when you’re bombarded with so many options in such a short time. \",\"user\",[120]],[\"s59\",\"d4\",716,853,\"Ultimately, that experience left me feeling both exhausted and frustrated, which is quite different from the enjoyment I had anticipated.\",\"user\",[120]],[\"s65\",\"d5\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 51–52 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s66\",\"d5\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s67\",\"d5\",105,503,\"User: However, I've realized that I needed to step back from blogging. In recent months, I found that the joy of sharing my thoughts on literature was overshadowed by the pressure to produce content consistently. Each time I sat down to write, instead of feeling excited about a new discovery in a book, I often felt weighed down by expectations, both my own and those I perceived from my readers. \",\"user\",[51]],[\"s68\",\"d5\",503,802,\"It got to the point where I was dreading my writing sessions rather than looking forward to them, which really highlighted how far I had drifted from my original passion. It was a tough decision to make, but stepping back from blogging has allowed me to rediscover that enthusiasm in different ways.\",\"user\",[51]],[\"s69\",\"d5\",802,815,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s70\",\"d5\",815,1098,\"Assistant: It's important to enjoy the process of engaging with literature, and it sounds like you've made a thoughtful decision based on your experiences. Taking a step back can be a very mature move, especially when it helps rekindle your passion for reading and discussing books. \",\"assistant\",[52]],[\"s71\",\"d5\",1098,1452,\"Focusing on direct interactions with friends can lead to more fulfilling conversations where you can share insights and differing perspectives in a more intimate setting. There's something special about verbal exchanges that can often enhance understanding and enjoyment of literature, as the spontaneity of conversation can lead to unexpected insights. \",\"assistant\",[52]],[\"s72\",\"d5\",1452,1787,\"So what specific topics or books have you been discussing with your friends recently? I'm curious to know what strides you've made in deepening those connections and how they compare to your previous experiences with blogging, as well as any new insights you may have gained about works that you thought you already understood well. ])\",\"assistant\",[52]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"history_evidence\",\"summary_revision_contracts\":{\"current_constraints\":{\"previous_version\":1,\"eligible_route_ids\":[\"fact_fde86a26e64f6b0b731d2b8f\"],\"required_source_ids\":[\"s14\",\"s32\",\"s57\",\"s3\",\"s59\",\"s30\",\"s58\",\"s4\",\"s31\",\"s13\"]}},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:a44ca93f001b14f6deabf95915b96c89c456b33307f339d168dbc79bb582865b\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":53.0,\"observed_end\":54.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d2\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:f62437d2b5820b60e98e323c1f0c71ca06601dba246a55a821cb967eadaa7c58\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":32.0,\"observed_end\":33.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d3\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:145c31806a41a34ea6d17afb883cfb2fb3fb61be4432f586e5cbd1d0f9251690\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":40.0,\"observed_end\":41.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d4\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:6575d48b8d8b63ae7661274604c5387697e6df77658d5abc891caf20f889a67f\",\"t